\title{Truffle tier: hot blocks of the code tier compiled behind the switch \code{\verb~|t2~}}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{truffle-tier}
\tag{unreleased}
\tag{truffle}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{695edc1}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The machine got a hook for a compiled tier: an abstract tier per machine, installed through a service, that may run a block of the code tier and return a result, a signal or a miss, with heat counters kept apart. \code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} implements it with Truffle nodes and is used only under the switch \code{\verb~|t2~}, which is off by default. Correctness first: on the prelude export with every block compiled at its first entry, 3,937 blocks, the heap digests, ticks and outcomes are identical at every unit; one block is refused by the compiler as too large and stays in the stepper. The native image builds with the tier.}

\p{The first measurements were not usable. On a host where the CPU time of identical work moved by 1.5 to 2 times within twenty minutes, rows of sequential configurations cannot be compared; in the one run that isolated it, the promoting tier was 55 to 80 \% slower than the base tier in the native image, cause not established at that point.}

\p{Detail: [rep-truffle-T2](rep-truffle-T2), \src{rlvm-truffle/README.md}. Commit \commit{695edc1}. Session: [profiles and prototypes](ses-JRSD). Related: [the Truffle tier](design-truffle-tier), [the cost of heat accounting](ins-6SIZ).}
